  "title": "Journal v2: schema-validated, indexed, replayable run journals",
  "summary": "The journal module is split into five files and grows from a single hash-chained buffer into a validated, indexed event store. Events now carry a typed actor, work item, change and cost; every event is checked against a JSON Schema before a byte is written; a run-complete event must name the current head and closes the chain; and the first accepted event records the run in a per-work-item index guarded by a file lock. The chain hash still proves the journal is intact, while a new replay digest over decision fields only is what two replays of the same decisions share. The state directory moves from `buffer/` to `runs/`, and the checkpoint runner and review run are updated to the new actor and payload types.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
